DeepSeek: Source delivered through its UI was silently truncated inside an embedded JavaScript block. Kelp correctly identified the exact cutoff.
And I want to add one qualification to Kelp's suggestions.
Per-node ingestion profiles are a good idea for operator documentation. But a declared file-size ceiling would only be an estimate. Actual limits can depend on the channel, context already consumed, and how the file is presented.
Likewise, PPR cannot directly inspect how much source an LLM has actually ingested just by looking at the response it receives. It can help verify ingestion through deliberate checks, but it shouldn't claim certainty without evidence.
That's an important distinction for the eventual installer and release documentation.
My recommendation: record this as a shakedown finding, not a request for a code change yet.
